# LifeOS Console

Run your workspace agents as a **team you chat with in Discord**, locally on your machine. Post a task
in a project channel; **Jarvis** (your chief-of-staff orchestrator) opens a thread, delegates to the
right agents, and they work **in that thread as themselves** while you watch and jump in. No API key,
no public server — everything runs through your Claude **subscription** via the Agent SDK.

> Status: built and typecheck-verified. **Not yet run live** — it needs one Discord application per
> bot (tokens). Follow *Setup* below to bring it online.

---

## The model

- **One bot per role/name — 20 bots.** Shared roles (`architect`, `feature-dev`, `infra-ops`,
  `qa-verify`) are a single bot each that serves every project; the **project context is resolved by
  the channel** the bot is working in. The other 16 agents are one bot each. `jarvis` is the
  orchestrator.
- **Channels are project-scoped.** On startup Jarvis creates `#general` + one channel per project.
  A bot working in `#accessbuddy` runs as that project's overlay; in `#lifesaveroncall`, that one.
- **Jarvis is the single front door.** Post a task in a project channel → Jarvis opens a **thread**,
  triages, and **delegates in dependency phases** (architecture → build → test). Agents in one phase
  run **in parallel** (the same role can run multiple instances), each posts its work **into the
  thread under its own name**, and Jarvis summarises. You have oversight in one place and can reply
  in-thread to steer, or let it run.
- **Talk to one agent directly:** `@mention` any bot in a channel/thread, or DM it.
- **Gated + autonomous:** read-only tools run freely; edits/shell/delegation/memory-writes prompt
  **Approve / Always / Deny**. `/autopilot` lets a bot act without asking (destructive/outbound
  actions and memory writes still confirm). Threads remember across turns (session resume).

### Agent definitions — train a role once

```
~/Documents/workspace/
  _bases/<role>/base.md                     # shared role definition (persona, method, memory protocol)
  projects/<project>/agents/<name>/
    claude.md                               # overlay: `base: <role>` + project specifics  (or a full def if unique)
    memory.md                               # what this agent has learnt
    context/                                # optional agent-specific working files
  projects/<project>/context/*.md           # project foundation (read by every agent in the project)
  personal/agents/jarvis/claude.md          # the orchestrator (`orchestrator: true`)
```

A shared role's system prompt is composed as **shared base → project overlay → memory → project
context**. Edit `_bases/architect/base.md` once and every project's architect inherits it. Agents are
discovered anywhere in the workspace tree (`*/agents/<name>/claude.md`).

